From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:41:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015-x: Describe the Wi-Fi port

The iPhone X has a BCM4357 on APCIE port 3. The runtime ADT gives the
port's CLKREQ# as GPIO 163, PERST# as GPIO 167 and the device-wake line
as GPIO 40, and the port's DART is dart-apcie3.

The h9p driver hides ports that are not enabled from config space and the
host bridge renumbers buses, so with only this port enabled it enumerates
as bus 1 and its requester ID is 0x100. The iommu-map entry follows that,
with a 0xff00 mask so every function of the port is mapped.

The port is active only once the controller is enabled on the d221 board,
with dart-apcie3. The port is labelled port03 so the board file can add
the endpoint under it, which the power-control patch that follows does; the BCM4357 enumerates as 14e4:440a.

[Orchard: labelled the root port port03 for the board's endpoint node]
Signed-off-by: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-x.dtsi | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-x.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-x.dtsi
index 41134ed..21abe9e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-x.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-x.dtsi
@@ -11,3 +11,29 @@
 / {
 	chassis-type = "handset";
 };
+
+&apcie {
+	iommu-map = <0x100 &dart_apcie3 0 0x0 0x80000000 0x0 0x3ffff000 1>;
+	iommu-map-mask = <0xff00>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&wifi_clkreq>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+	port03: pci@3,0 {
+		device_type = "pci";
+		reg = <0x1800 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+		bus-range = <1 1>;
+		max-link-speed = <2>;
+		apple,manual-availability-iommu = <&dart_apcie3 0>;
+		reset-gpios = <&pinctrl_ap 167 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+		#address-cells = <3>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+	};
+};
+
+&pinctrl_ap {
+	wifi_clkreq: wifi-clkreq-pins {
+		pinmux = <APPLE_PINMUX(163, 1)>;
+	};
+};
